]


###
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 7. MEDICINE UNITS  (UoM attached to specific medicines)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# After migration, every medicine already has Tablet (base+default)
# and Strip (if tabletsPerStrip>1) units created automatically.

### 7a. Get all units for medicine 1 (management view)
GET {{base}}/api/medicineunit/by-medicine/1
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmacistToken}}

###
### 7b. Get units for POS dropdown — default first
GET {{base}}/api/medicineunit/pos/1
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmacistToken}}

###
### 7c. Attach a Box unit to medicine 1 (10 strips per box = 100 tablets)
POST {{base}}/api/medicineunit
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "medicineId": 1,
  "unitOfMeasureId": 7,
  "conversionFactorToBase": 100,
  "unitPrice": 450.00,
  "isBaseUnit": false,
  "isDefault": false
}

###
### 7d. Set Strip as the default POS unit for medicine 1
POST {{base}}/api/medicineunit/set-default
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "medicineId": 1,
  "medicineUnitId": 2
}

###
### 7e. Update the price for a medicine unit (unit ID 2 = Strip of medicine 1)
PATCH {{base}}/api/medicineunit/2/price
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "unitPrice": 50.00
}

###
### 7f. Get POS units for medicine 2 — should show default first
GET {{base}}/api/medicineunit/pos/2
Authorization: Bearer {{pharmacistToken}}


